  "group": "owned",
  "title": "owned, redis, through, relaxed",
  "summary": "A shared Redis with a recorded maxmemory and allkeys-lru policy (approximate LRU, and the report says so). Write-through: the new value is never published before the database commit; the writer tombstones, commits, then republishes only the committed representation. A reader may receive an older committed value than the latest acknowledged write, and every such read is counted. The owned model supplies a monotonic cache_version to fence and validate against.",
  "risk": "may return stale committed data; throughput is only reportable with the wrong-read count and rate beside it",
